concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-10 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 Issue of warrants"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-10 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A magistrate must issue a warrant, in the statutory form, for a person’s arrest if an application is made, in the statutory form, on behalf of the Tribunal, for issue of a warrant pursuant to the notice. (2) A magistrate must issue a warrant, in the statutory form, for a person’s arrest if: (a) an application is made, in the statutory form, on behalf of a Tribunal, for issue of a warrant otherwise than pursuant to such a notice; and (b) the application is accompanied by a copy of an arrest warrant for the person that was issued by the Tribunal; and (c) the application contains a statement to the effect that, because of circumstances of urgency, it is necessary to issue a warrant   Surrender of persons to a Tribunal  Part 3 Arrest of persons  Division 1 Section 11 International War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995 Compilation date: 28/03/2026 before receiving a notice from the Attorney-General under section 9. (3) The magistrate must without delay send to the Attorney-General a report stating whether the magistrate has issued the warrant. Note: Division 4 of Part 7 deals with matters relating to arrest." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A magistrate must issue a warrant, in the statutory form, for a person’s arrest if an application is made, in the statutory form, on behalf of the Tribunal, for issue of a warrant pursuant to the notice. (2) A magistrate must issue a warrant, in the statutory form, for a person’s arrest if: (a) an application is made, in the statutory form, on behalf of a Tribunal, for issue of a warrant otherwise than pursuant to such a notice; and (b) the application is accompanied by a copy of an arrest warrant for the person that was issued by the Tribunal; and (c) the application contains a statement to the effect that, because of circumstances of urgency, it is necessary to issue a warrant   Surrender of persons to a Tribunal  Part 3 Arrest of persons  Division 1 Section 11 International War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995 Compilation date: 28/03/2026 before receiving a notice from the Attorney-General under section 9. (3) The magistrate must without delay send to the Attorney-General a report stating whether the magistrate has issued the warrant. Note: Division 4 of Part 7 deals with matters relating to arrest."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e1df8047b7925ed24100887b299076a4ec95e98dddb43571ba36f6dad720eece" ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-10-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-10-ss-2 ;
