concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-20 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20 Detention following surrender warrants"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-20 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the Attorney-General issues the surrender warrant, the person must be brought as soon as practicable before a magistrate in the State or Territory in which the person is on remand.   Surrender of persons to a Tribunal  Part 3 Surrender of persons  Division 2 Section 21 International War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995 Compilation date: 28/03/2026 (2) A magistrate must remand the person in custody for such period or periods as may be necessary to enable the warrant to be executed." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the Attorney-General issues the surrender warrant, the person must be brought as soon as practicable before a magistrate in the State or Territory in which the person is on remand.   Surrender of persons to a Tribunal  Part 3 Surrender of persons  Division 2 Section 21 International War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995 Compilation date: 28/03/2026 (2) A magistrate must remand the person in custody for such period or periods as may be necessary to enable the warrant to be executed."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fa7fb558b517f25a376478a673bbc3cea193c2a4e633d2c72fba424697a1a453" ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-20-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-20-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf> ;
    dc:source "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.28" .
