concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-21 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21 Content of surrender warrants"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-21 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A surrender warrant in relation to the person (the eligible person) must: (a) require the person in whose custody the eligible person is being held to release the eligible person into the custody of a police officer; and (b) authorise the police officer to transport the eligible person in custody, and, if necessary or convenient, to detain the eligible person in custody, for the purpose of enabling the eligible person: (i) to be placed in the custody of a specified person who is an officer of the Tribunal or other person authorised by the Tribunal; and (ii) to be transported to a place specified by the Tribunal; and (c) authorise the specified person to transport the eligible person in custody to a place specified by the Tribunal for the purpose of surrendering the eligible person to a person appointed by the Tribunal to receive the person. (2) A place referred to in paragraph (1)(b) or (c) may be a place in or outside Australia." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A surrender warrant in relation to the person (the eligible person) must: (a) require the person in whose custody the eligible person is being held to release the eligible person into the custody of a police officer; and (b) authorise the police officer to transport the eligible person in custody, and, if necessary or convenient, to detain the eligible person in custody, for the purpose of enabling the eligible person: (i) to be placed in the custody of a specified person who is an officer of the Tribunal or other person authorised by the Tribunal; and (ii) to be transported to a place specified by the Tribunal; and (c) authorise the specified person to transport the eligible person in custody to a place specified by the Tribunal for the purpose of surrendering the eligible person to a person appointed by the Tribunal to receive the person. (2) A place referred to in paragraph (1)(b) or (c) may be a place in or outside Australia."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4075caca5a5c6c791664ae6baab5397b94e615faffc150cc7bab39ebadfd6b4c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "29"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-21-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-21-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf> ;
    dc:source "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.29" .
