    values:originalText "(2) In this section: Tribunal immunity certificate means a certificate or declaration that: (a) is given or made by a Tribunal under the Statute of the Tribunal or under the rules adopted under the Statute of the Tribunal; and (b) specifies or declares that, under the Statute of the Tribunal or under the rules adopted under the Statute of the Tribunal, persons generally or a specified person could or could not: (i) either generally or in specified proceedings; and (ii) either generally or in specified circumstances; be required to answer a specified question or to produce a specified document.   Other forms of assistance to a Tribunal  Part 4 Requests for surveillance devices  Division 1A Section 32A International War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995 Compilation date: 28/03/2026" ;
