    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The Attorney-General must not comply with the request if, in his or her opinion: (a) complying with the request would prejudice Australia’s sovereignty, security or national interest; or (b) there are special circumstances justifying non-compliance.   Other forms of assistance to a Tribunal  Part 4 Giving evidence at hearings, or assisting in investigations, in foreign countries  Division Section 36 International War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995 Compilation date: 28/03/2026" ;
