    skos:definition "(2) Subject to subsection (4), if the prisoner is being held in custody, the Attorney-General may: (a) if the prisoner is a federal prisoner and is not also a State prisoner-direct that the prisoner be released from prison for the purpose of travelling to the foreign country to give evidence at the proceeding or to assist the investigation; and (b) if the prisoner is a federal prisoner and also a State prisoner-direct, subject to the obtaining of any approvals required to be obtained from an authority of the relevant State, that the prisoner be released from prison for the purpose of such travel; and (c) in any case-subject to the making or giving of any necessary directions or approvals relevant to release of the prisoner, make arrangements for such travel in the custody of a police"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "dfcf460ee3fef9ce072a938f070fff402f4f78fe60572fafb4ad54b189dd6c4e" ;
