concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40am a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "40AM Failing to comply with a notice"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-40am ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is given a notice under section 40AH; and (b) the person fails to comply with the notice. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 100 penalty units, or both.   Other forms of assistance to a Tribunal  Part 4 Identification, tracing, and freezing or seizure, of proceeds of Tribunal offences" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is given a notice under section 40AH; and (b) the person fails to comply with the notice. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 100 penalty units, or both.   Other forms of assistance to a Tribunal  Part 4 Identification, tracing, and freezing or seizure, of proceeds of Tribunal offences"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ef68fa5868c1c1717345f2f16614394dd9b2b04f2a73ec4214e649ffaccd2d7d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "58"^^xsd:integer ;
