concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40au a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "40AU Dealing with evidential material and certain property or"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-40au ;
    values:originalText "things seized under POCA search warrants (1) This section applies if: (a) property or a thing (the seized item) is seized under a POCA search warrant in relation to a Tribunal offence; and (b) the seized item is: (i) evidential material; or (ii) property or a thing of a kind referred to in subparagraph 40AR(a)(iv); and (c) the seized item is seized by a person (the seizing officer) who is: (i) an authorised officer; or (ii) a person assisting in relation to the warrant. (2) The seizing officer may retain the seized item for a period not exceeding 1 month pending a written direction from the Attorney-General as to how to deal with the seized item. (3) Without limiting the directions that may be given under subsection (2), the Attorney-General may direct the seizing officer to send the seized item to the Tribunal." ;
    skos:definition "things seized under POCA search warrants (1) This section applies if: (a) property or a thing (the seized item) is seized under a POCA search warrant in relation to a Tribunal offence; and (b) the seized item is: (i) evidential material; or (ii) property or a thing of a kind referred to in subparagraph 40AR(a)(iv); and (c) the seized item is seized by a person (the seizing officer) who is: (i) an authorised officer; or (ii) a person assisting in relation to the warrant. (2) The seizing officer may retain the seized item for a period not exceeding 1 month pending a written direction from the Attorney-General as to how to deal with the seized item. (3) Without limiting the directions that may be given under subsection (2), the Attorney-General may direct the seizing officer to send the seized item to the Tribunal."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "61e9bb2be232e039264e3061e24b8e6634f4bfb7f851d87062ac54abf3eba7f4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "65"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40au-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40au-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40au-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf> ;
    dc:source "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.65" .
doc:sec-40au a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "40AU Dealing with evidential material and certain property or" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "things seized under POCA search warrants (1) This section applies if: (a) property or a thing (the seized item) is seized under a POCA search warrant in relation to a Tribunal offence; and (b) the seized item is: (i) evidential material; or (ii) property or a thing of a kind referred to in subparagraph 40AR(a)(iv); and (c) the seized item is seized by a person (the seizing officer) who is: (i) an authorised officer; or (ii) a person assisting in relation to the warrant. (2) The seizing officer may retain the seized item for a period not exceeding 1 month pending a written direction from the Attorney-General as to how to deal with the seized item. (3) Without limiting the directions that may be given under subsection (2), the Attorney-General may direct the seizing officer to send the seized item to the Tribunal." ;
    cof:pageNumber "65"^^xsd:integer .

