concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-42 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "42 Tribunal’s powers while sitting in Australia"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-42 ;
    values:originalText "(1) While a Tribunal is sitting in Australia, it may exercise such powers as are prescribed by the regulations in respect of the Tribunal. (2) Regulations made for the purposes of subsection (1) must implement agreements between the Commonwealth and the Tribunal about the powers that the Tribunal may exercise while sitting in Australia. (3) Despite section 14 of the Legislation Act 2003, regulations made for the purposes of subsection (1) may apply, adopt or incorporate, with or without modification, the rules of procedure and evidence, as in force at a particular time or as in force from time to time, adopted under: (a) in the case of the Former Yugoslavia Tribunal—Article 15 of the Statute of the Tribunal; or (b) in the case of the Rwanda Tribunal—Article 14 of the Statute of the Tribunal; or   Sittings of a Tribunal in Australia  Part 5  Section 43 International War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995 Compilation date: 28/03/2026 (c) in the case of the International Residual Mechanism for Criminal Tribunals—Article 13 of the Statute of the Tribunal. 43  Contravention of Tribunal orders etc. A person must not: (a) intentionally contravene an order that a Tribunal makes while sitting in Australia; or (b) otherwise intentionally hinder a Tribunal in performing its functions while sitting in Australia. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years. Note: Under subsection 4D(1) of the Crimes Act 1914, this penalty is only a maximum penalty for the offence.  Subsection 4B(2) of that Act allows a court to impose an appropriate fine instead of, or in addition to, a term of imprisonment. If a body corporate is convicted of the offence, subsection 4B(3) of that Act allows a court to impose a fine of an amount not greater than 5 times the maximum fine that the court could impose on an individual convicted of the same offence." ;
    skos:definition "(1) While a Tribunal is sitting in Australia, it may exercise such powers as are prescribed by the regulations in respect of the Tribunal. (2) Regulations made for the purposes of subsection (1) must implement agreements between the Commonwealth and the Tribunal about the powers that the Tribunal may exercise while sitting in Australia. (3) Despite section 14 of the Legislation Act 2003, regulations made for the purposes of subsection (1) may apply, adopt or incorporate, with or without modification, the rules of procedure and evidence, as in force at a particular time or as in force from time to time, adopted under: (a) in the case of the Former Yugoslavia Tribunal—Article 15 of the Statute of the Tribunal; or (b) in the case of the Rwanda Tribunal—Article 14 of the Statute of the Tribunal; or   Sittings of a Tribunal in Australia  Part 5  Section 43 International War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995 Compilation date: 28/03/2026 (c) in the case of the International Residual Mechanism for Criminal Tribunals—Article 13 of the Statute of the Tribunal. 43  Contravention of Tribunal orders etc. A person must not: (a) intentionally contravene an order that a Tribunal makes while sitting in Australia; or (b) otherwise intentionally hinder a Tribunal in performing its functions while sitting in Australia. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years. Note: Under subsection 4D(1) of the Crimes Act 1914, this penalty is only a maximum penalty for the offence.  Subsection 4B(2) of that Act allows a court to impose an appropriate fine instead of, or in addition to, a term of imprisonment. If a body corporate is convicted of the offence, subsection 4B(3) of that Act allows a court to impose a fine of an amount not greater than 5 times the maximum fine that the court could impose on an individual convicted of the same offence."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "22fb89f51b0ec9907ce1ad1ba829b26ca33f75a1390e6043263d1d16e54b2040" ;
    cof:pageNumber "66"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-42-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-42-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-42-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf> ;
    dc:source "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.66" .
