doc:sec-46-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "46(1) Effect of order" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A forfeiture order registered in a court has effect, and may be enforced, as if it were a forfeiture order made by the court under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 at the time of registration." ;
    cof:pageNumber "69"^^xsd:integer .

concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-46-ss-1a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "46(1A) Effect of order"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-46-ss-1a ;
    values:originalText "(1A) In particular, section 68 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 applies in relation to the forfeiture order as if: (a) the reference in subparagraph 68(1)(b)(i) of that Act to a proceeds of crime authority having applied for the order were a reference to the authority having applied for registration of the order under section 45 of this Act; and (b) subparagraph 68(1)(b)(ii) of that Act were repealed." ;
    skos:definition "(1A) In particular, section 68 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 applies in relation to the forfeiture order as if: (a) the reference in subparagraph 68(1)(b)(i) of that Act to a proceeds of crime authority having applied for the order were a reference to the authority having applied for registration of the order under section 45 of this Act; and (b) subparagraph 68(1)(b)(ii) of that Act were repealed."@en ;
