doc:sec-58-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "58(3) Use of electronic equipment at premises" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Equipment may be seized under paragraph (2)(a) only if: (a) it is not practicable to put the material in documentary form as mentioned in paragraph (2)(b) or to copy the material as mentioned in paragraph (2)(c); or (b) possession by the occupier of the equipment could constitute an offence against an Australian law." ;
    cof:pageNumber "82"^^xsd:integer .

concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-58-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "58(4) Use of electronic equipment at premises"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-58-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If the executing officer or an officer assisting believes on reasonable grounds that: (a) evidential material may be accessible by operating electronic equipment at the warrant premises; and (b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and (c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the material may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered with; he or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment, whether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise." ;
    skos:definition "(4) If the executing officer or an officer assisting believes on reasonable grounds that: (a) evidential material may be accessible by operating electronic equipment at the warrant premises; and (b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and (c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the material may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered with; he or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment, whether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "48ac4065c7ef8771244c046ccb40502637126724ba653d938534f64ee3742207" ;
    values:partOf concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-58 ;
    cof:pageNumber "82"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Executing officer may take necessary actions to secure electronic equipment at premises." ;
