concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-59 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "59 Compensation for damage to electronic equipment"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-59 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If: (a) damage is caused to equipment as a result of it being operated as mentioned in section 57 or 58; and (b) the damage was caused as a result of: (i) insufficient care being exercised in selecting the person who was to operate the equipment; or (ii) insufficient care being exercised by the person operating the equipment; compensation for the damage is payable to the owner of the equipment. (2) Compensation is payable out of money appropriated by the Parliament for the purpose. (3) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to be had to whether the occupier of the warrant premises and his or her employees and agents, if they were available at the time, had provided any warning or guidance as to the operation of the equipment that was appropriate in the circumstances.   Search, seizure and powers of arrest  Part 7 Provisions relating to execution of search warrants  Division 2 Section 60 International War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995 Compilation date: 28/03/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If: (a) damage is caused to equipment as a result of it being operated as mentioned in section 57 or 58; and (b) the damage was caused as a result of: (i) insufficient care being exercised in selecting the person who was to operate the equipment; or (ii) insufficient care being exercised by the person operating the equipment; compensation for the damage is payable to the owner of the equipment. (2) Compensation is payable out of money appropriated by the Parliament for the purpose. (3) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to be had to whether the occupier of the warrant premises and his or her employees and agents, if they were available at the time, had provided any warning or guidance as to the operation of the equipment that was appropriate in the circumstances.   Search, seizure and powers of arrest  Part 7 Provisions relating to execution of search warrants  Division 2 Section 60 International War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995 Compilation date: 28/03/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "29eaebe3438fa16cb199eb25d0b946c1755f620f754b7139496181f017270944" ;
    cof:pageNumber "84"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-59-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-59-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-59-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf> ;
    dc:source "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.84" .
doc:sec-59 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "59 Compensation for damage to electronic equipment" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If: (a) damage is caused to equipment as a result of it being operated as mentioned in section 57 or 58; and (b) the damage was caused as a result of: (i) insufficient care being exercised in selecting the person who was to operate the equipment; or (ii) insufficient care being exercised by the person operating the equipment; compensation for the damage is payable to the owner of the equipment. (2) Compensation is payable out of money appropriated by the Parliament for the purpose. (3) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to be had to whether the occupier of the warrant premises and his or her employees and agents, if they were available at the time, had provided any warning or guidance as to the operation of the equipment that was appropriate in the circumstances.   Search, seizure and powers of arrest  Part 7 Provisions relating to execution of search warrants  Division 2 Section 60 International War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995 Compilation date: 28/03/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "84"^^xsd:integer .

