concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-76 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "76 Offences relating to telephone warrants"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-76 ;
    values:originalText "A person must not: (a) state in a document that purports to be a form of warrant under section 52 the name of a magistrate unless that magistrate issued the warrant; or (b) state on a form of warrant under that section a matter that, to the person’s knowledge, departs in a material particular from the form authorised by the magistrate; or (c) purport to execute, or present to a person, a document that purports to be a form of warrant under that section that: (i) the person knows has not been approved by a magistrate under that section; or (ii) the person knows to depart in a material particular from the terms authorised by a magistrate under that section; or (d) send to a magistrate a form of warrant under that section that is not the form of warrant that the person purported to execute. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years. Note: Under subsection 4D(1) of the Crimes Act 1914, this penalty is only a maximum penalty for the offence.  Subsection 4B(2) of that Act allows a court to impose an appropriate fine instead of, or in addition to, a term of imprisonment." ;
    skos:definition "A person must not: (a) state in a document that purports to be a form of warrant under section 52 the name of a magistrate unless that magistrate issued the warrant; or (b) state on a form of warrant under that section a matter that, to the person’s knowledge, departs in a material particular from the form authorised by the magistrate; or (c) purport to execute, or present to a person, a document that purports to be a form of warrant under that section that: (i) the person knows has not been approved by a magistrate under that section; or (ii) the person knows to depart in a material particular from the terms authorised by a magistrate under that section; or (d) send to a magistrate a form of warrant under that section that is not the form of warrant that the person purported to execute. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years. Note: Under subsection 4D(1) of the Crimes Act 1914, this penalty is only a maximum penalty for the offence.  Subsection 4B(2) of that Act allows a court to impose an appropriate fine instead of, or in addition to, a term of imprisonment."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "227779591c91fd4b0ec37fffa431f1962e1b33e1c16830ba667a7de677325225" ;
    cof:pageNumber "96"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Prohibits certain actions related to telephone warrants." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf> ;
    dc:source "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.96" ;
    cml:asserts concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-76-norm .
